# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend environment variables (Vite). Copy to .env.local for local dev.
# .env.local is gitignored — never commit real phone numbers to a public repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Map demo counters (by the first word of the counter name) to real WhatsApp
# test numbers so the "Send on WhatsApp" button opens a real chat. Without this,
# hero counters use synthetic seed numbers and WhatsApp may show
# "not on WhatsApp".
#
# Format: digits only, INCLUDING country code, no "+" / spaces / dashes.
#   India example: 919876543210  (91 + 10-digit number)
#
# Keys below match the five hero counters:
#   Gateway  -> Gateway Jetty — Counter 3 (ferry, Mumbai)
#   BEST     -> BEST Depot — Wadala Counter 1 (bus, Mumbai)
#   Sahakari -> Sahakari Bhandar — Dadar (retail, Mumbai)
#   Metro    -> Metro Line-1 Andheri — TVM Cluster (metro, Mumbai)
#   Shree    -> Shree Provision Stores — Pune (retail, Pune)
#
# Set the real values in .env.local locally, and in your Vercel project's
# Environment Variables for the deployed demo.
VITE_DEMO_PHONES={"Gateway":"910000000000","BEST":"910000000000","Sahakari":"910000000000","Metro":"910000000000","Shree":"910000000000"}
